{"text": "State of Connecticut\n\nKATHARINE L WADE\nINSURANCE COMMISSIONER\n\nPO Box 816\nHARTFORD CT 06142 0816\n\nHartford\n\nJanuary 6, 2017\n\nThe Honorable Kevin McCarthy\nMajority Leader\nUS House of Representatives\nWashington, DC 20515\n\nDear Majority Leader McCarthy\n\nI appreciate the opportunity to share Connecticut\u2019s perspective on next steps our state and our nation\ncan take together as we continue to build upon the successes of the Affordable Care Act (ACA)\nSince 2011, Connecticut\u2019s uninsured rate has gone from 8 percent to a historic low of 3 8 percent\nApproximately 110,000 Connecticut residents have obtained coverage through our state-sponsored\nmarketplace and the expansion of Medicaid provided coverage for more than 200,000 Connecticut\nresidents\n\nThe ACA has provided all Americans with greater access to health insurance and they are using their\ncoverage for preventive care and other medical treatment Rather than repeal the law, Congress\nshould improve it There are three areas that we can focus on to improve going forward \u2014 market\nstability, the regulatory environment and state flexibility, and cost contamment\n\nMarket Stability\nA key area that we need to focus on 1s stabilizing the markets for consumers and employers and the\ninsurers providing coverage, particularly in the individual market Keeping certain popula: aspects\nof the law while removing others which are less popular but critical for a stable, functioning\ninsurance market must be carefully considered We need to continue to protect consumers with\npreexisting health conditions while incentivizing healthy people to maintain continuity of coverage\nThis 1s necessary to create balanced risk pools, a key attribute of successfully functioning insurance\nmarkets\n\nAnother area which 1s tmportant to market stability 1s encouraging innovation and flexibility in\nproduct design This will provide more choices for consumers and greater competition and will offer\nthe potential to lower premium rates Greater choice and competition 1s a hallmark of consumer\nprotection It drives competition and fosters innovation Allowing more flexibility in plan design will\nencourage all demographics of our nation \u2014 from single, healthy millennials to growing families to\nolder Americans still in our workforce \u2014 to choose an insurance plan that best meets their individual\nand family needs",
